{"id":"man","name":"Man","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:man","torrey:man"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Man","text":"(1.) Heb. ‘Adam, used as the proper name of the first man. The name is derived from a word meaning “to be red,” and thus the first man was called Adam because he was formed from the red earth. It is also the generic name of the human race (Gen. 1:26, 27; 5:2; 8:21; Deut. 8:3). Its equivalents are the Latin homo and the Greek anthropos (Matt. 5:13, 16). It denotes also man in opposition to woman (Gen. 3:12; Matt. 19:10). (2.) Heb. ‘ish, like the Latin vir and Greek aner, denotes properly a man in opposition to a woman (1 Sam. 17:33; Matt. 14:21); a husband (Gen. 3:16; Hos. 2:16); man with reference to excellent mental qualities. (3.) Heb. ‘enosh, man as mortal, transient, perishable (2 Chr. 14:11; Isa. 8:1; Job 15:14; Ps. 8:4; 9:19, 20; 103:15). It is applied to women (Josh. 8:25). (4.) Heb. geber, man with reference to his strength, as distinguished from women (Deut. 22:5) and from …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G4151","lemma":"πνεῦμα","xlit":"pneûma","gloss":"a current of air","kjv":"ghost, life, spirit, mind","count":23,"share":0.07},{"strong":"H85","lemma":"אַבְרָהָם","xlit":"ʼAbrâhâm","gloss":"Abraham, the later name of Abram","kjv":"Abraham","count":14,"share":0.05},{"strong":"G2309","lemma":"θέλω","xlit":"thélō","gloss":"to determine properly denotes rather a passive acquiesce","kjv":"desire, be disposed, intend, list","count":14,"share":0.05},{"strong":"H7307","lemma":"רוּחַ","xlit":"rûwach","gloss":"wind","kjv":"air, anger, blast, breath","count":15,"share":0.05},{"strong":"H8064","lemma":"שָׁמַיִם","xlit":"shâmayim","gloss":"the sky","kjv":"air, astrologer, heaven","count":15,"share":0.05},{"strong":"H1588","lemma":"גַּן","xlit":"gan","gloss":"a garden","kjv":"garden","count":9,"share":0.03}],"verses":["Matt.26.41","Mark.14.38","Luke.23.46","Luke.24.39","John.3.5","John.3.6","John.3.8","John